{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Fighting the Competition"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Setting up the Meeting"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Grammar - part 1 > Living Longer and Better"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le09ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Pronouncing Weak Forms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In English, we have two different types of words: <br/>a) <span class=\"strong\">grammatical</span> or <span class=\"strong\">function</span> words and <br/>b) <span class=\"strong\">content</span> words. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Content</span> words are adjectives, adverbs, nouns and verbs. They are often stressed in spoken English. <span class=\"strong\">Grammatical</span> words, on the other hand, are small words that basically help us build sentences and connect  <span class=\"strong\">content</span>  words and do not carry any meaning. Articles, prepositions, conjunctions, auxiliary verbs, and determiners are all examples of <span class=\"strong\">grammatical</span> words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In spoken English, these words have no stress and are often weak. In other words, they are not pronounced as <span class=\"strong\">content</span>  words, which are strongly pronounced (\u201cstrong form\u201d) and are often pronounced with a schwa sound. This is why they are difficult to hear when people are speaking."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the following sentences, the weak forms are underlined."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Mr. Gibbs office. How <span class=\"underline\">can</span> I help you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Could</span> I speak <span class=\"underline\">to</span> Michael, please?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'd like <span class =\"underline\">to</span> arrange <span class =\"underline\">an</span> appointment <span class =\"underline\">for</span> Maria <span class =\"underline\">to</span> see him."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Managing a Phone Conversation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Talking on the telephone can be challenging for a variety of reasons. Firstly, you are not able to see the person you're talking to, so there's no body language to be read. Secondly, it requires a special set of words, phrases, and expressions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The chart below will help you to speak on the phone confidently in business and personal situations."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Answering the phone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">For calls to your direct line</span><br/><ul><li><span class =\\\"italic\\\">Good morning, this is Hannah. </span></li><li><span class =\\\"italic\\\">Good morning, Polygon firm. Hannah speaking. How can I help you?</span></li></li><span class =\\\"italic\\\"><li>Farmani's office, Hannah speaking.</span></li></ul><span class=\\\"underline\\\">For calls to a general number</span><br><ul><li><span class =\\\"italic\\\">Thank you for calling Polygon. How may I direct your call?</span></li></ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Introducing yourself\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">When calling a general number</span><ul><span class =\\\"italic\\\"><li>May I speak with Janet Ellison?</li><li>Hello, this is Brianne Smith calling for Janet Ellison.</li><li>Is Janet Ellison in?</li></span></ul>  \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Connecting someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you don't understand the caller\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">When you answer the phone and it is for someone else</span><ul><span class =\\\"italic\\\"><li>One minute, I'll transfer you.</li><li>Please hold and I'll put you through.</li><li>One moment, please.</li><li>Just a moment. Can I put you on hold?</li></span></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>Could you please repeat that?</li><li>I'm sorry, I didn't catch that.</li><li>I didn't catch what you just said.</li><li>Can you speak a little more slowly?</li></ul></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">NOTE:</span><br/>When talking about using the telephone, note the prepositions we use:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">on the phone (=talking using the telephone)</span>:<br/><span class =\"italic\">I'm on the phone with Mr. Farmani.<br/>Most teenagers spend hours on the phone every day.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">by phone/over the phone (=using the telephone)</span>:<br/><span class =\"italic\">We are doing business over the phone.<br/>We take orders by phone or by email.</span></li></ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "available"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not busy and has enough time to talk to you"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is he available next week?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you set up an appointment on the telephone."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "scattered"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "spread over a long period of time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Tuesday's appointments are rather scattered. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "status update"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "information about a situation at a particular time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can you give me a status update?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "awkward"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "difficult to do"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That could be awkward. What about in the morning? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "feasible"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is possible and is likely to work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is 4:00 p.m. feasible? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob04aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you have to call an office to make an appointment. Write a dialogue between you and the receptionist. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to manage the phone conversation. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Set up an appointment with a manager. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to include all the necessary information. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "End the phone conversation. "}, {"type": "text", "content":